# Kernel releases (uname -r) that `make install` accepts without MOOB_ALLOW_UNSUPPORTED=1, and
# the only releases DKMS builds for (packaging/debian/rules turns this list into
# BUILD_EXCLUSIVE_KERNEL). The rule is docs/compatibility.md section 1: a kernel is supported
# when the full suite and the KASAN job pass on it in CI, with one fstests quick run per lower
# filesystem (rule 3). Three series: Debian 13's 6.12 builds, Debian's 7.3.3 (sid on 2026-11-09,
# journal 0277) and Ubuntu 26.04's 7.0 (journal 0281); on 7.0 and 7.3 the layer module only, the
# M1 module (kernel/) stays 6.12-only. The upstream 6.12.116, 7.0.14 and 7.3.3 KASAN kernels are
# test builds, not installation targets, so they are not listed. One entry per line: an exact
# release, or (Ubuntu only, ADR-0036) a series whose one '*' stands for one or more digits, the
# ABI number. 7.0.0-*-generic was tested on 7.0.0-43-generic; .github/workflows/ubuntu-drift.yml
# builds weekly against the newest release of the series.
6.12.111+deb13-amd64
6.12.113+deb13-amd64
6.12.115+deb13.1-amd64
7.3.3+deb14-amd64
7.0.0-*-generic
